<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33374" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeŏnes</span></b> , um,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παίονες</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of
			Macedonia</i>, <i>in that part of it afterwards called
				Emathia</i>, <i>the Pœonians</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 2,
				2, 77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. M. 5, 313</span></i>.—<i>Sing.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeŏn</span></b> , ŏnis,
				m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παίων</span>, <i>a Pœonian</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 42,
				51, 6</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeŏnĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παιονία</span>, <i>the country of the
				Pœonians</i>, <i>Emathia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 10,
				17, § 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 40,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeŏnis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>a
				female Pœonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeonis Euippe mater fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 303</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeŏnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παιόνιος</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pœonia</i>, <i>Pœonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 10, 17, § 35</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
